WEBVTT

NOTE willdan weekly, 2026-09-02. Four speakers, thirty-one minutes; the
NOTE cues below are the part the flywheel's meeting adapter reads.

1
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:29.400
<v Chuck>The provider client is still the thing that bites us. Two hosts
came up on Sunday and both wrote to the same provider inside a minute.

2
00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:41.900
<v Dana>That is the one-writer claim, isn't it. We wrote it down and then
never built the lease on that path.

3
00:04:41.900 --> 00:05:03.100
<v Chuck>We wrote it down for the atlas side. Switchboard has its own
client and nothing says only one of them writes.

4
00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:20.600
<v Priya>Then the claim is scoped wrong rather than missing. It attaches
to the atlas element and it should attach to the contract between them.

5
00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:38.000
<v Dana>Rescoping it makes switchboard's ledger cell unjudged, which is
what we want. Planning picks it up on the next run.

6
00:11:47.200 --> 00:12:04.800
<v Marcus>Separate thing: the status rows lose their numbers after a
merge lands. It is cosmetic but it makes the morning read useless.

7
00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:19.300
<v Chuck>That is a chore, not an intent. File it against atlas and let it
ride with whatever bolt is open.

8
00:26:31.500 --> 00:26:52.700
<v Priya>Last one. The retry bound on build is three and we hit it twice
this week on the same item, both times for a flaky fixture.

9
00:26:52.700 --> 00:27:09.000
<v Chuck>Flaky fixture is its own finding. Do not raise the bound to hide
it.
